    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "The draft is intense, which is good for the base, but some of the language might be too much for the moderate voters. They're worried about the cost of that kind of police funding and the idea that stricter sentencing just fills up jails without actually fixing the root causes of crime. How would you address those critics in the speech without losing the \"tough on crime\" edge?",
