      "content": "To appeal to moderates without softening your core message, you must frame increased funding not merely as salaries, but as an investment in technology and specialized training that saves money over time by preventing recidivism. You should explicitly acknowledge valid concerns about jail populations by positioning property crime prevention and restorative justice programs alongside stricter sentencing as a dual strategy that secures our streets while healing our communities. This approach allows you to retain your \"tough on crime\" edge by arguing that true safety requires both a strong deterrent for violent offenders and the resources to build a safer, more prosperous future for everyone.",
